    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Baxter equation\nThe old conventions (`old-conventions/XXX-CG/L1-mathcalA.tex`) had, on $Q=z^{x/h}q$:\n$\\nu_1(x)\\nu_1(x-h)\\nu_1(x-2h)Q(x+h)-t_1\\,\\nu_1(x-h)\\nu_1(x-2h)Q(x)+t_2\\,\\nu_1(x-2h)Q(x-h)-t_3Q(x-2h)=0$, with $t_3=\\chi_3\\,\\nu_1(x-2h)\\nu_2(x-h)\\nu_3(x)$ and $\\nu_n=u-\\theta-h\\lambda_n$.\n\nThe first step is the new quantum determinant, which fixes where the $\\nu$ dressing goes.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* tG[3] should be χ[3] times a scalar quantum determinant; read off its ν-factorization *)\nqdetNew = Simplify[tG[3][u]];\nToString[{Union[Flatten[Simplify[qdetNew - qdetNew[[1, 1]]*IdentityMatrix[8]]]], Factor[qdetNew[[1, 1]]/χ[3]], Table[ν[n][u], {n, 3}]}, InputForm]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"758596\" data-output-id=\"9\" data-out-n=\"86\" data-sub-idx=\"2\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"30\" data-sub-start=\"2\" data-sub-end=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[86]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7XHtcezBcfSwgLSgodSAtICRcdGhldGEkWzFdKSooMipoICsgdSAtICRcdGhldGEkWzFdKSooMipoIC0gdSArICRcdGhldGEkWzFdKSksIFx7MipoICsgdSAtICRcdGhldGEkWzFdLCBoICsgdSAtICRcdGhldGEkWzFdLCB1IC0gJFx0aGV0YSRbMV1cfVx9fQ==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">{{0}, -((u - </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">[1])*(2*h + u - </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">[1])*(2*h - u + </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">[1])), {2*h + u - </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">[1], h + u - </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">[1], u - </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">[1]}}</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[86]= \\text{\\{\\{0\\}, -((u - $\\theta$[1])*(2*h + u - $\\theta$[1])*(2*h - u + $\\theta$[1])), \\{2*h + u - $\\theta$[1], h + u - $\\theta$[1], u - $\\theta$[1]\\}\\}}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "1c53a764-c269-42cd-a82c-b5655d7ec364"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "Result: $t^G_3=\\chi_3\\,\\nu_1(u)\\nu_2(u-h)\\nu_3(u-2h)$ with the new $\\nu_n=u-\\theta+h\\lambda_n$. The old one was $\\chi_3\\nu_1(u-2h)\\nu_2(u-h)\\nu_3(u)$ with the old $\\nu$.\n\nNext, compute the eigenvalues at a numeric point (old point 1, which is unimodular) and scan for polynomial solutions $q$, with $Q=z_i^{\\pm x/h}q$, of two candidate operators:\n- **old**: the old form, with the new $\\nu_1$;\n- **mirror**: the old form under $h\\to-h$, with $t_a$ re-shifted to the new quantum-minor convention, i.e. $\\nu_1(x)\\nu_1(x+h)\\nu_1(x+2h)Q(x-h)-t_1(x)\\nu_1(x+h)\\nu_1(x+2h)Q(x)+t_2(x+h)\\nu_1(x+2h)Q(x+h)-t_3(x+2h)Q(x+2h)$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* numeric points: 1 = old point 1 (unimodular, χ3=1); 2 = same h,θ but χ3 = 7/2, to test the χ3 dependence *)\nptList = {{h -> 1, θ[1] -> 1/3, z[1] -> 5/2, z[2] -> 7/3, z[3] -> 6/35}, {h -> 1, θ[1] -> 1/3, z[1] -> 5/2, z[2] -> 7/3, z[3] -> 3/5}};\nptSel = 2;\nptB = ptList[[ptSel]];\nprecB = 60;\n(* t1 alone is degenerate on the 2-dim zero-weight space, so diagonalize a generic combination of t1 and t2 *)\nClearAll[tGn];\ntGn[a_] := tGn[a] = Expand[tG[a][u] /. ptB];\nmixB = N[(tGn[1] + Pi*tGn[2]) /. u -> 3/7, precB];\nevecB = Eigenvectors[mixB];\n(* eigenvalue polynomials t_a(u) for each state, read off from the largest component *)\neigvalB = Table[With[{k = Ordering[Abs[ψ], -1][[1]]}, Table[Chop[Expand[(N[tGn[a], precB] . ψ)[[k]]/ψ[[k]]], 10^-40], {a, 3}]], {ψ, evecB}];\n(* weight in the twist-diagonal frame: Pphys.t1.Pphys^-1 = Σ z_i ℒ_ii, so the Cartan there is Pphys^-1.E_ii.Pphys *)\nwtB = Table[Chop[Table[With[{v = N[Inverse[Pphys /. ptB] . Ee[1][i, i] . (Pphys /. ptB), precB] . ψ, k = Ordering[Abs[ψ], -1][[1]]}, v[[k]]/ψ[[k]]], {i, 3}], 10^-30], {ψ, evecB}];\nToString[{ptSel, χ[3] /. ptB, Length[evecB], Round[wtB]}, InputForm]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"758596\" data-output-id=\"106\" data-out-n=\"745\" data-sub-idx=\"14\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"32\" data-sub-start=\"14\" data-sub-end=\"14\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[745]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7XHsyLCA3LzIsIDgsIFx7XHswLCAyLCAxXH0sIFx7MSwgMSwgMVx9LCBcezIsIDAsIDFcfSwgXHswLCAxLCAyXH0sIFx7MSwgMCwgMlx9LCBcezEsIDEsIDFcfSwgXHsyLCAxLCAwXH0sIFx7MSwgMiwgMFx9XH1cfX0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">{2, 7/2, 8, {{0, 2, 1}, {1, 1, 1}, {2, 0, 1}, {0, 1, 2}, {1, 0, 2}, {1, 1, 1}, {2, 1, 0}, {1, 2, 0}}}</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[745]= \\text{\\{2, 7/2, 8, \\{\\{0, 2, 1\\}, \\{1, 1, 1\\}, \\{2, 0, 1\\}, \\{0, 1, 2\\}, \\{1, 0, 2\\}, \\{1, 1, 1\\}, \\{2, 1, 0\\}, \\{1, 2, 0\\}\\}\\}}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "5d05c8e5-2eaf-47c5-9262-f5e2e667976b"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ν1B[x_] := ν[1][x] /. ptB;\n(* candidate Baxter operators acting on Q, given the eigenvalue polynomials tt={t1,t2,t3} in u *)\nbaxOp[\"old\", tt_, Q_, x_] := ν1B[x] ν1B[x - 1] ν1B[x - 2] Q[x + 1] - (tt[[1]] /. u -> x) ν1B[x - 1] ν1B[x - 2] Q[x] + (tt[[2]] /. u -> x) ν1B[x - 2] Q[x - 1] - (tt[[3]] /. u -> x) Q[x - 2];\nbaxOp[\"mirror\", tt_, Q_, x_] := ν1B[x] ν1B[x + 1] ν1B[x + 2] Q[x - 1] - (tt[[1]] /. u -> x) ν1B[x + 1] ν1B[x + 2] Q[x] + (tt[[2]] /. u -> x + 1) ν1B[x + 2] Q[x + 1] - (tt[[3]] /. u -> x + 2) Q[x + 2];\n(* smallest degree d<=5 of a polynomial q with Q=zz^(s x) q solving the operator (h=1); -1 if none.\n   An identically vanishing residual gives CoefficientList[0]={}, which counts as solved. *)\npolyDeg[op_, tt_, zz_, s_] := Module[{c, q, eqs, d, res = -1},\n  Do[If[res < 0,\n    q[y_] := Sum[c[j] y^j, {j, 0, d}];\n    eqs = CoefficientList[Chop[Expand[baxOp[op, tt, Function[y, zz^(s y) q[y]], X]/zz^(s X)], 10^-40], X];\n    If[eqs === {} || Length[NullSpace[N[Table[Coefficient[e, c[j]], {e, eqs}, {j, 0, d}], precB], Tolerance -> 10^-30]] > 0, res = d]], {d, 0, 5}]; res];\nscanB = Table[{Round[wtB[[A]]], Table[polyDeg[op, eigvalB[[A]], z[i] /. ptB, s], {op, {\"old\", \"mirror\"}}, {s, {1, -1}}, {i, 3}]}, {A, 8}];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[Flatten[{Row[r[[1]], \",\"], Map[Row[#, \",\"] &, Flatten[r[[2]], 1]]}], {r, scanB}], {\"weight μ\", \"old z^+\", \"old z^-\", \"mirror z^+\", \"mirror z^-\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
