  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (numeric, point 1, adjoint, L=1).** In the new conventions the direct Baxter equation is the old one under $h\\to-h$:\n$$\\nu_1(x)\\nu_1(x+h)\\nu_1(x+2h)\\,Q(x-h)-t_1(x)\\,\\nu_1(x+h)\\nu_1(x+2h)\\,Q(x)+t_2(x+h)\\,\\nu_1(x+2h)\\,Q(x+h)-t_3(x+2h)\\,Q(x+2h)=0,$$\nwith $\\nu_n(x)=x-\\theta+h\\lambda_n$ and $t_a$ the eigenvalues of `tG[a]`. The asymptotics flip: $Q_i=z_i^{-x/h}q_i$ with $\\deg q_i=\\lambda_1-\\mu_i$, which holds for all 8 states, including both $(1,1,1)$ states. Here $\\mu$ is the weight in the twist-diagonal frame, $\\mathrm{Pphys}^{-1}E_{ii}\\mathrm{Pphys}$.\n\nThe old operator (with the new $\\nu_1$) has no polynomial solutions for either $z^{\\pm x/h}$, and neither does the mirror operator with $z^{+x/h}$.\n\nNot done yet: the dual equation ($Q^j$), other reps, a second numeric point, and a symbolic check.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Dual Baxter equation\nThe old dual equation, written on $Q^j=z_j^{-x/h}q^j$, was\n$\\nu_3(x+h)\\nu_3(x+2h)\\nu_3(x+3h)Q(x)-t_1(x+h)\\nu_3(x+2h)\\nu_3(x+3h)Q(x+h)+t_2(x+2h)\\nu_3(x+3h)Q(x+2h)-t_3(x+3h)Q(x+3h)=0$, with $\\deg q^j=\\mu_j$.\n\nThe mirror candidate applies the same map that worked for the direct equation: $h\\to-h$, then $t_a^{\\rm old}(u)\\to t_a^{\\rm new}(u+(a-1)h)$. This gives\n$\\nu_3(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)\\nu_3(x-3h)Q(x)-t_1(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)\\nu_3(x-3h)Q(x-h)+t_2(x-h)\\nu_3(x-3h)Q(x-2h)-t_3(x-h)Q(x-3h)=0$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ν3B[x_] := ν[3][x] /. ptB;\nbaxOp[\"dualOld\", tt_, Q_, x_] := ν3B[x + 1] ν3B[x + 2] ν3B[x + 3] Q[x] - (tt[[1]] /. u -> x + 1) ν3B[x + 2] ν3B[x + 3] Q[x + 1] + (tt[[2]] /. u -> x + 2) ν3B[x + 3] Q[x + 2] - (tt[[3]] /. u -> x + 3) Q[x + 3];\nbaxOp[\"dualMirror\", tt_, Q_, x_] := ν3B[x - 1] ν3B[x - 2] ν3B[x - 3] Q[x] - (tt[[1]] /. u -> x - 1) ν3B[x - 2] ν3B[x - 3] Q[x - 1] + (tt[[2]] /. u -> x - 1) ν3B[x - 3] Q[x - 2] - (tt[[3]] /. u -> x - 1) Q[x - 3];\n(* same scan as the direct case: smallest deg q^j with Q^j = z_j^(s x) q^j; -1 if none *)\nscanDualB = Table[{Round[wtB[[A]]], Table[polyDeg[op, eigvalB[[A]], z[j] /. ptB, s], {op, {\"dualOld\", \"dualMirror\"}}, {s, {1, -1}}, {j, 3}]}, {A, 8}];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[Flatten[{Row[r[[1]], \",\"], Map[Row[#, \",\"] &, Flatten[r[[2]], 1]]}], {r, scanDualB}], {\"weight μ\", \"dualOld z^+\", \"dualOld z^-\", \"dualMirror z^+\", \"dualMirror z^-\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
