  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (dual, numeric, point 1, adjoint, L=1).** The dual equation is again the old one mirrored ($h\\to-h$, $t_a(u)\\to t_a(u+(a-1)h)$):\n$$\\nu_3(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)\\nu_3(x-3h)\\,Q(x)-t_1(x-h)\\,\\nu_3(x-2h)\\nu_3(x-3h)\\,Q(x-h)+t_2(x-h)\\,\\nu_3(x-3h)\\,Q(x-2h)-t_3(x-h)\\,Q(x-3h)=0,$$\nwith $Q^j=z_j^{+x/h}q^j$ and $\\deg q^j=\\mu_j$, which holds for all 8 states. The old dual form has no polynomial solutions for either sign.\n\n**QQ relation.** For all 8 states and all cyclic $(a,b;c)$:\n$$Q_a(u)Q_b(u+h)-Q_b(u)Q_a(u+h)=\\Big(\\tfrac1{z_b}-\\tfrac1{z_a}\\Big)\\,\\nu_1(u)\\,Q^c(u),$$\nwith the $q$'s monic and residual 0. This mirrors the old $Q_{ab}=(1/z_b-1/z_a)F_\\lambda Q^c$, with $F_\\lambda=u-\\theta-2h\\to u-\\theta+2h$. The shift in $Q_{ab}$ is now $+h$; it was $-h$. Presumably $F_\\lambda=\\prod_{n=\\lambda_2+1}^{\\lambda_1}(u-\\theta+nh)$ in general, but this is untested beyond the adjoint.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Transfer-matrix eigenvalues as Wronskians of the dual Q's\nThe dual equation in uniform form ($x\\to x+h$) is\n$\\nu_3(x)\\nu_3(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)Q(x+h)-t_1(x)\\nu_3(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)Q(x)+t_2(x)\\nu_3(x-2h)Q(x-h)-t_3(x)Q(x-2h)=0$.\n\nLet $D_{k_1k_2k_3}(x)=\\det_{j,c}Q^j(x+k_ch)$. The $4\\times4$ determinant with rows $Q^1,Q^2,Q^3,Q$ and column shifts $(+h,0,-h,-2h)$ vanishes for $Q=Q^{1,2,3}$. Expanding it along the last row and matching to the equation gives\n$$t_1=\\nu_3(x)\\frac{D_{1,-1,-2}}{D_{0,-1,-2}},\\qquad t_2=\\nu_3(x)\\nu_3(x-h)\\frac{D_{1,0,-2}}{D_{0,-1,-2}},\\qquad t_3=\\nu_3(x)\\nu_3(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)\\frac{D_{1,0,-1}}{D_{0,-1,-2}}.$$",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* row j of the Casoratian with the z_j^(x/h) prefactor stripped: Q^j(x+k h)/z_j^(x/h) = z_j^k q^j(x+k) at h=1 *)\ncasD[qu_, ks_] := Expand[Det[Table[zB[[j]]^k (qu[[j]] /. X -> X + k), {j, 3}, {k, ks}]]];\n(* check D_{0,-1,-2} t_a == ν-prefactor * D_a as polynomials in X, for every state *)\nwronB = Table[Module[{tt = eigvalB[[A]] /. u -> X, qu, d0, d1, d2, d3},\n   qu = Table[monicQ[\"dualMirror\", eigvalB[[A]], zB[[j]], 1, scanDualB[[A, 2, 2, 1, j]]], {j, 3}];\n   d0 = casD[qu, {0, -1, -2}]; d1 = casD[qu, {1, -1, -2}]; d2 = casD[qu, {1, 0, -2}]; d3 = casD[qu, {1, 0, -1}];\n   {Round[wtB[[A]]], N[Max[Abs[CoefficientList[Expand[#], X]]] & /@ {d0 tt[[1]] - ν3B[X] d1, d0 tt[[2]] - ν3B[X] ν3B[X - 1] d2, d0 tt[[3]] - ν3B[X] ν3B[X - 1] ν3B[X - 2] d3}, 3],\n    (* the shift-covariant Casoratian itself: expect a constant times (x-θ-h)(x-θ)(x-θ+h) for the adjoint *)\n    Chop[N[X - θ[1] /. ptB /. NSolve[d3 == 0, X], 8], 10^-20]}], {A, 8}];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{Row[r[[1]], \",\"], Row[Chop[r[[2]], 10^-25], \" | \"], Row[r[[3]], \", \"]}, {r, wronB}], {\"weight μ\", \"residuals t1 | t2 | t3\", \"roots of D_{1,0,-1} in x-θ\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
