xt\"><span class=\"mord\">, </span></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:10.8em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-5.15em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-9.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-10.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-12.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-13.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[766]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{weight $\\mu$} & \\text{residuals t1 | t2 | t3} & \\text{roots of D\\_\\{1,0,-1\\} in x-$\\theta$}\\\\\\hline0,2,1 & 0\\text{ | }0\\text{ | }0 & -2.\\,\\text{, }-1.\\,\\text{, }0\\\\\\hline1,1,1 & 0\\text{ | }0\\text{ | }0 & -2.\\,\\text{, }-1.\\,\\text{, }0\\\\\\hline2,0,1 & 0\\text{ | }0\\text{ | }0 & -2.\\,\\text{, }-1.\\,\\text{, }0\\\\\\hline0,1,2 & 0\\text{ | }0\\text{ | }0 & -2.\\,\\text{, }-1.\\,\\text{, }0\\\\\\hline1,0,2 & 0\\text{ | }0\\text{ | }0 & -2.\\,\\text{, }-1.\\,\\text{, }0\\\\\\hline1,1,1 & 0\\text{ | }0\\text{ | }0 & -2.\\,\\text{, }-1.\\,\\text{, }0\\\\\\hline2,1,0 & 0\\text{ | }0\\text{ | }0 & -2.\\,\\text{, }-1.\\,\\text{, }0\\\\\\hline1,2,0 & 0\\text{ | }0\\text{ | }0 & -2.\\,\\text{, }-1.\\,\\text{, }0\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "582eb805-fad3-4a07-b217-c2bf970e344c"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (numeric, point 1, adjoint).** All three Wronskian formulas hold as exact polynomial identities ($D_{0,-1,-2}\\,t_a-\\nu\\text{-prefactor}\\cdot D_a\\equiv0$) for all 8 states, with the monic dual $q$'s.\n\nThe Casoratian is also fixed by the representation: $D_{1,0,-1}(x)\\propto\\nu_1(x)\\nu_2(x)\\nu_3(x)$, with roots at $x-\\theta=-2,-1,0$. Since $D_{0,-1,-2}(x)=D_{1,0,-1}(x-h)/\\chi_3$, the $t_3$ formula reproduces the quantum determinant $\\chi_3\\nu_1(x)\\nu_2(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)$.\n\nCaveat: point 1 has $\\chi_3=1$, so the $\\chi_3$ factor itself has not been tested numerically.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**$\\chi_3\\neq1$ check.** Cells 33–42 were rerun at `ptSel = 2` ($h=1$, $\\theta=1/3$, $z=(5/2,7/3,3/5)$, $\\chi_3=7/2$). Every result above survives unchanged:\n- the mirror direct and dual equations, with the same degree rules; the old forms and wrong-sign asymptotics still give nothing;\n- QQ, with residual 0 and constant exactly $1/z_b-1/z_a$; the exponentials now carry an extra overall $\\chi_3^{-u/h}$, which the polynomial check strips;\n- the Wronskian formulas for $t_{1,2,3}$, with residual 0, which confirms the $\\chi_3$ in $D_{0,-1,-2}(x)=D_{1,0,-1}(x-h)/\\chi_3$.\n\nSo nothing in the Baxter, QQ or Wronskian structure needs unimodular twist. The notebook is saved with `ptSel = 2`; set `ptSel = 1` to reproduce the unimodular run.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### CBR formula and its Wronskian form\n**CBR.** $T_\\lambda(u)=\\det_{1\\le i,j\\le\\lambda_1}T_{\\lambda'_j+i-j}(u+h(i-1))$, with $T_0=1$ and $T_a=0$ for $a<0$ or $a>3$. The stored `t[{a,b}]` matrices are exactly these, for example $t_{\\{2,1\\}}=t_2(u)t_1(u+h)-t_3(u+h)$.\n\n**Guess.** The $t_a$ results above suggest\n$$T_\\lambda(x)=P_\\lambda(x)\\,\\frac{D_{\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2-1,\\lambda_3-2}}{D_{0,-1,-2}},$$\na quantum Weyl character formula. The guess for the prefactor is the content product $P_\\lambda=\\prod_{(r,c)\\in\\lambda}\\nu_3(x+(c-r)h)$, which reproduces $P$ for $t_{1,2,3}$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* CBR determinant on eigenvalue polynomials tt = {t1,t2,t3}(u), at the numeric point (h from ptB) *)\ncbrT[tt_, lam_, x_] := Module[{lp = DeleteCases[lam, 0], n, lc, ta, hh = h /. ptB},\n  ta[a_, y_] := Which[a == 0, 1, a < 0 || a > 3, 0, True, tt[[a]] /. u -> y];\n  n = If[lp === {}, 0, First[lp]];\n  lc = Table[Count[lp, _?(# >= j &)], {j, n}];\n  If[n == 0, 1, Expand[Det[Table[ta[lc[[j]] + i - j, x + (i - 1) hh], {i, n}, {j, n}]]]]];\n(* check 1: CBR on eigenvalues reproduces the eigenvalues of the stored t[{a,b}] matrices, on every state *)\ncbrCheck = Table[Max[Table[With[{m = N[t[ab][u] /. ptB, precB], ψ = evecB[[A]]}, With[{k = Ordering[Abs[ψ], -1][[1]]},\n      Max[Abs[CoefficientList[Chop[Expand[(m . ψ)[[k]]/ψ[[k]] - cbrT[eigvalB[[A]], ab, u]], 10^-35], u]], 0]]], {A, 8}]], {ab, {{1, 0}, {1, 1}, {2, 0}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}}}];\nToString[{\"CBR vs stored t[{a,b}], max residual per {10,11,20,21,22}:\", N[cbrCheck, 3]}, InputForm]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"758596\" data-output-id=\"112\" data-out-n=\"769\" data-sub-idx=\"4\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"45\" data-sub-start=\"9\" data-sub-end=\"9\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[769]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7XHtcQ0JSIHZzIHN0b3JlZCB0W1x7YSxiXH1dLCBtYXggcmVzaWR1YWwgcGVyIFx7MTAsMTEsMjAsMjEsMjJcfTpcLCBcezAsIDAsIDAsIDAsIDBcfVx9fQ==\"><span class=\"wolfbook-render-error\" style=\"color:#cc0000;font-family:monospace;white-space:pre-wrap\">[LaTeX error] KaTeX parse error: Undefined control sequence: \\CBR at position 9: \\text{\\{\\̲C̲B̲R̲ ̲vs stored t[\\{a…<br><small>\\text{\\{\\CBR vs stored t[\\{a,b\\}], max residual per \\{10,11,20,21,22\\}:\\, \\{0, 0, 0, 0, 0\\}\\}}</small></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
