   "metadata": {
    "toolId": "X64sZmlsZQ"
   }
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (adjoint, point with $\\chi_3=7/2$).**\n- **CBR.** It reproduces the eigenvalues of every stored `t[{a,b}]` ($\\{1,0\\},\\{1,1\\},\\{2,0\\},\\{2,1\\},\\{2,2\\}$) on all 8 states, with residual 0.\n- **Wronskian form.** For all 19 $\\lambda\\subseteq3\\times3$:\n$$T_\\lambda(x)=\\prod_{(r,c)\\in\\lambda}\\nu_3\\big(x+(c-r)h\\big)\\;\\frac{\\det_{j,k}Q^j\\big(x+(\\lambda_k-k+1)h\\big)}{\\det_{j,k}Q^j\\big(x+(1-k)h\\big)}.$$\n  - The remainder is exactly 0 in every case.\n  - The prefactor is identical across all 8 states.\n  - The prefactor equals the content product exactly.\n\nThis is the quantum Weyl character formula. Each box of content $c-r$ contributes a $\\nu_3$ shifted by $(c-r)h$, and the $Q^j$ shifts are $\\lambda_k-k+1$. With $\\lambda=(1,0,0),(1,1,0),(1,1,1)$ it reduces to the $t_{1,2,3}$ formulas above.\n\nCaveat: the adjoint has $\\lambda_3=0$, so $\\nu_3$ and $(x-\\theta)$ coincide. Run $\\lambda_3\\neq0$ to tell them apart.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Evaluating at $x=\\theta-2h$: degenerate columns\nThe SoV-basis construction needs $T_\\lambda(\\theta-2h)$. Write $v(p)=(Q^1,Q^2,Q^3)(p)$ for the columns of the Casoratians, with $z_j^{\\theta/h}$ stripped from each row. At special points $p=\\theta+mh$ the dual equation loses terms, so columns can become parallel or dependent. Scan $m\\in[-6,4]$ for every state.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* column at p = θ + m h, with row prefactor z_j^(θ/h) stripped: z_j^m q^j(θ+m) (h=1) *)\nquB = Table[monicQ[\"dualMirror\", eigvalB[[A]], zB[[j]], 1, scanDualB[[A, 2, 2, 1, j]]], {A, 8}, {j, 3}];\ncolB[A_, m_] := Table[zB[[j]]^m (quB[[A, j]] /. X -> (θ[1] /. ptB) + m), {j, 3}];\nmRange = Range[-6, 4];\n(* zero columns, parallel pairs (all 2x2 minors vanish), dependent triples (det vanishes); keep those present in EVERY state *)\ndegB = Table[{\n    Select[mRange, Norm[colB[A, #]] < 10^-30 &],\n    Select[Subsets[mRange, {2}], Norm[Flatten[Minors[Transpose[{colB[A, #[[1]]], colB[A, #[[2]]]}], 2]]] < 10^-30 &],\n    Select[Subsets[mRange, {3}], Abs[Det[colB[A, #] & /@ #]] < 10^-30 &]}, {A, 8}];\ndegCommon = Table[Intersection @@ degB[[All, k]], {k, 3}];\nToString[{\"zero cols:\", degCommon[[1]], \"parallel pairs:\", degCommon[[2]], \"dependent triples:\", degCommon[[3]]}, InputForm]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"758596\" data-output-id=\"114\" data-out-n=\"779\" data-sub-idx=\"7\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"49\" data-sub-start=\"10\" data-sub-end=\"10\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[779]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"wolfbook-render-error\" style=\"color:#cc0000;font-family:monospace;white-space:pre-wrap\">[LaTeX error] KaTeX parse error: Undefined control sequence: \\zero at position 9: \\text{\\{\\̲z̲e̲r̲o̲ ̲cols:\\, \\{\\}, \\…<br><small>\\text{\\{\\zero cols:\\, \\{\\}, \\parallel pairs:\\, \\{\\{-1, 0\\}\\}, \\dependent triples:\\, \\{\\{-6, -1, 0\\}, \\{-5, -1, 0\\}, \\{-4, -1, 0\\}, \\{-3, -2, -1\\}, \\{-3, -2, 0\\}, \\{-3, -1, 0\\}, \\{-2, -1, 0\\}, \\{-1, 0, 1\\}, \\{-1, 0, 2\\}, \\{-1, 0, 3\\}, \\{-1, 0, 4\\}\\}\\}}</small></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[779]= \\text{\\{\\zero cols:\\, \\{\\}, \\parallel pairs:\\, \\{\\{-1, 0\\}\\}, \\dependent triples:\\, \\{\\{-6, -1, 0\\}, \\{-5, -1, 0\\}, \\{-4, -1, 0\\}, \\{-3, -2, -1\\}, \\{-3, -2, 0\\}, \\{-3, -1, 0\\}, \\{-2, -1, 0\\}, \\{-1, 0, 1\\}, \\{-1, 0, 2\\}, \\{-1, 0, 3\\}, \\{-1, 0, 4\\}\\}\\}}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "8ac99fe2-b81e-4321-8567-ff2ffae78a15"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {
    "toolId": "Y100sZmlsZQ"
   }
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "Result of the scan, identical in all 8 states: $v(\\theta-h)\\parallel v(\\theta)$, and $v(\\theta-3h),v(\\theta-2h),v(\\theta-h)$ are dependent. So $v(\\theta+mh)$ for $m=-3,\\dots,0$ all lie in one 2-plane $\\Pi$.\n\nAt $x=\\theta-2h$ the numerator columns sit at $m=(\\lambda_1-2,\\lambda_2-3,\\lambda_3-4)$ and the denominator columns at $m=(-2,-3,-4)$. This predicts:\n- **$\\lambda_3=0$, $\\lambda_1\\le2$.** $T_\\lambda(\\theta-2h)=P_\\lambda\\,\\dfrac{\\det_2[Q^{j}(\\theta+(\\lambda_1-2)h),\\,Q^{j}(\\theta+(\\lambda_2-3)h)]}{\\det_2[Q^{j}(\\theta-2h),\\,Q^{j}(\\theta-3h)]}$, for any choice of two rows $j$. The factor normal to $\\Pi$ in $v(\\theta-4h)$ cancels.\n- **$\\lambda_3\\ge1$.** $T_\\lambda(\\theta-2h)=0$, since all three columns lie in $\\Pi$.\n- **$\\lambda_1=3$.** $T_\\lambda(\\theta-2h)=0$, since $P_\\lambda\\ni\\nu_3(\\theta)=0$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* compare CBR T_λ(θ-2h) with the predicted 2x2 formula (all three row pairs) or with 0 *)\nx0B = (θ[1] /. ptB) - 2;\nmin2[A_, {m1_, m2_}, rows_] := Det[Table[colB[A, m][[j]], {j, rows}, {m, {m1, m2}}]];\nred2B = Table[Module[{cbr, pred},\n    cbr = Table[cbrT[eigvalB[[A]], lam, x0B], {A, 8}];\n    pred = Table[If[lam[[3]] == 0 && lam[[1]] <= 2,\n       Table[contentP[lam, x0B] min2[A, {lam[[1]] - 2, lam[[2]] - 3}, rows]/min2[A, {-2, -3}, rows], {rows, {{1, 2}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}}}],\n       {0, 0, 0}], {A, 8}];\n    {lam, N[Max[Abs[cbr]], 3], N[Max[Abs[Flatten[pred - cbr]]], 3]}], {lam, lamList}];\nGrid[Prepend[red2B, {\"λ\", \"max |T_λ(θ-2h)|\", \"max |prediction - CBR|\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
