      {
       "data": "Out[783]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline\\lambda  & \\text{max |T\\_$\\lambda$($\\theta$-2h)|} & \\text{max |prediction - CBR|}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,0,0\\right\\} & 7.33 & 0.\\times 10^{-55}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1,0\\right\\} & 17.5 & 0.\\times 10^{-54}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1,1\\right\\} & 0.\\times 10^{-58} & 0.\\times 10^{-58}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,0,0\\right\\} & 18.3 & 0.\\times 10^{-54}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1,0\\right\\} & 43.8 & 0.\\times 10^{-54}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1,1\\right\\} & 0.\\times 10^{-116} & 0.\\times 10^{-116}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2,0\\right\\} & 6.70\\times 10^{-69} & 8.91\\times 10^{-65}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2,1\\right\\} & 0 & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2,2\\right\\} & 0 & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,0,0\\right\\} & 1.76\\times 10^{-68} & 1.76\\times 10^{-68}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,1,0\\right\\} & 1.54\\times 10^{-68} & 1.54\\times 10^{-68}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,1,1\\right\\} & 0 & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,2,0\\right\\} & 2.37\\times 10^{-68} & 2.37\\times 10^{-68}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,2,1\\right\\} & 0 & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,2,2\\right\\} & 0 & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,3,0\\right\\} & 5.92\\times 10^{-68} & 5.92\\times 10^{-68}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,3,1\\right\\} & 0 & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,3,2\\right\\} & 0 & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,3,3\\right\\} & 0 & 0\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "e6b653d4-d7ee-4a9d-9a93-096264aa5695"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (adjoint, $\\chi_3=7/2$).** The prediction matches CBR for all 19 $\\lambda$ and all 8 states, with residual 0, and every choice of two rows gives the same value.\n- **Nonzero cases.** $T_\\lambda(\\theta-2h)\\neq0$ only for $\\lambda=(1),(1,1),(2),(2,1)$. These are exactly the $t$'s used to build $\\langle x|$. $(2,2)$ vanishes because $v(\\theta)\\parallel v(\\theta-h)$. For these four,\n$$T_\\lambda(\\theta-2h)=P_\\lambda(\\theta-2h)\\,\\frac{\\det_2\\big[Q^j(\\theta+(\\lambda_1-2)h),\\,Q^j(\\theta+(\\lambda_2-3)h)\\big]}{\\det_2\\big[Q^j(\\theta-2h),\\,Q^j(\\theta-3h)\\big]}.$$\n- **Origin of $v(\\theta)\\parallel v(\\theta-h)$.** The uniform dual equation at $x=\\theta+h$ loses its first two terms (they contain $\\nu_3(\\theta)=0$), leaving $t_2(\\theta+h)\\nu_3(\\theta-h)\\,v(\\theta)=t_3(\\theta+h)\\,v(\\theta-h)$.\n- **Origin of the dependent triple.** The equation at $x=\\theta-h$ is a 4-term relation among $v(\\theta),\\dots,v(\\theta-3h)$, so with the parallel pair it makes $v(\\theta-3h),v(\\theta-2h),v(\\theta-h)$ dependent.\n\nThis is the adjoint only. How the 2-plane and its shifts depend on $\\lambda$ (presumably through $\\nu_3$ and the length of the $\\theta$-ladder) is still to be checked.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Matching norms (adjoint)\n- **Normalization.** $|\\Psi_A\\rangle$ are right eigenvectors normalized by $\\langle x_{\\{2\\},\\{2,1\\}}|\\Psi_A\\rangle=1$. $\\langle\\Psi_A|$ are right eigenvectors of the transposed $t$'s, normalized by $\\langle\\Psi_A|y_{\\{2\\},\\{2,1\\}}\\rangle=1$.\n- **SoV side.** $\\det N^{AB}$ is the new-conventions version from `Baxter-QQ-Wronskian.wb`. Its columns are $\\{-\\langle Q^jQ_i\\rangle_\\rho,\\ \\langle Q^jQ_i^{[2]}\\rangle_\\rho,\\ \\langle Q^{j[-2]}Q_i\\rangle_\\rho\\}$, its poles are at $\\theta-nh$ for $n=\\lambda_3..\\lambda_1$, and its rows are $(i,j)\\in\\{(1,3),(1,2),(2,3)\\}$, the old choice.\n- **Test.** The first candidate for the ratio is the old form mirrored under $h\\to-h$: $\\langle\\Psi_A|\\Psi_A\\rangle=\\kappa\\,\\det N^{AA}/(c^{\\rm ref}_A\\Psi^{\\rm ref}_A)$, with $\\Psi^{\\rm ref}=Q_1(\\theta-h)Q_{12}(\\theta)$ and $c^{\\rm ref}=Q^3(\\theta-h)[Q^3(\\theta-2h)Q^2(\\theta-3h)-Q^2(\\theta-2h)Q^3(\\theta-3h)]$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* bras and kets at the numeric point; bra matched to ket by the eigenvalue of the same generic t1/t2 combination *)\nx0N = N[Flatten[x[{{2}, {2, 1}}] /. ptB], precB];\ny0N = N[Flatten[y[{{2}, {2, 1}}] /. ptB], precB];\n{evalR, evecR} = Eigensystem[mixB];\n{evalL, evecL} = Eigensystem[Transpose[mixB]];\n(* keep the state ordering of evecB/eigvalB: match each evecB to its eigenvalue *)\nketN = Table[With[{v = evecB[[A]]}, v/(x0N . v)], {A, 8}];\nbraN = Table[With[{lam = (mixB . evecB[[A]])[[Ordering[Abs[evecB[[A]]], -1][[1]]]]/evecB[[A]][[Ordering[Abs[evecB[[A]]], -1][[1]]]]},\n    With[{w = evecL[[First[Ordering[Abs[evalL - lam], 1]]]]}, w/(w . y0N)]], {A, 8}];\ngramN = Table[braN[[A]] . ketN[[B]], {A, 8}, {B, 8}];\n(* SoV side: monic Q's, Q_i = z_i^(-x) q_i, Q^j = z_j^(+x) q^j (h=1) *)\nqdB = Table[monicQ[\"mirror\", eigvalB[[A]], zB[[i]], -1, scanB[[A, 2, 2, 2, i]]], {A, 8}, {i, 3}];\nQDn[A_, i_, xx_] := N[zB[[i]]^(-xx), precB] (qdB[[A, i]] /. X -> xx);\nQUn[A_, j_, xx_] := N[zB[[j]]^xx, precB] (quB[[A, j]] /. X -> xx);\nthN = θ[1] /. ptB; polesN = Range[0, 2];\nwN[n_] := 1/Product[(m - n), {m, DeleteCases[polesN, n]}];\nrowN[A_, B_, {i_, j_}] := Sum[With[{xx = thN - n}, wN[n] {-QUn[A, j, xx] QDn[B, i, xx], QUn[A, j, xx] QDn[B, i, xx + 1], QUn[A, j, xx - 1] QDn[B, i, xx]}], {n, polesN}];\ndetNN = Table[Det[rowN[A, B, #] & /@ {{1, 3}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}}], {A, 8}, {B, 8}];\noffR[m_] := N[Max[Abs[m - DiagonalMatrix[Diagonal[m]]]]/Min[Abs[Diagonal[m]]], 3];\n(* mirrored reference factors *)\npsiRefN[A_] := QDn[A, 1, thN - 1] (QDn[A, 1, thN] QDn[A, 2, thN + 1] - QDn[A, 2, thN] QDn[A, 1, thN + 1]);\ncRefN[A_] := QUn[A, 3, thN - 1] (QUn[A, 3, thN - 2] QUn[A, 2, thN - 3] - QUn[A, 2, thN - 2] QUn[A, 3, thN - 3]);\nratioN = Table[Diagonal[gramN][[A]]/Diagonal[detNN][[A]], {A, 8}];\nkapN = Table[ratioN[[A]] cRefN[A] psiRefN[A], {A, 8}];\nToString[{\"gram offdiag/diag:\", offR[gramN], \"detN offdiag/diag:\", offR[detNN], \"R_A spread:\", N[Max[Abs[ratioN/ratioN[[1]] - 1]], 3], \"kappa_A = R_A cref Psiref spread:\", N[Max[Abs[kapN/kapN[[1]] - 1]], 3], \"kappa_1:\", N[kapN[[1]], 12]}, InputForm]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"758596\" data-output-id=\"116\" data-out-n=\"803\" data-sub-idx=\"23\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"54\" data-sub-start=\"24\" data-sub-end=\"24\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[803]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"wolfbook-render-error\" style=\"color:#cc0000;font-family:monospace;white-space:pre-wrap\">[LaTeX error] KaTeX parse error: Expected &#39;}&#39;, got &#39;_&#39; at position 158: …wedge}$-55, \\&quot;R_̲A spread:\\&quot;, 31…<br><small>\\text{&quot;{\\&quot;gram offdiag/diag:\\&quot;, 0$\\grave{ }$$\\grave{ }$52.96075423641374, \\&quot;detN offdiag/diag:\\&quot;, 6.0295952989807176155569$\\grave{ }$3.*${}^{\\wedge}$-55, \\&quot;R_A spread:\\&quot;, 317484.6862887790767410005$\\grave{ }$3., \\&quot;kappa_A = R_A cref Psiref spread:\\&quot;, 14.1234567901234567901$\\grave{ }$3., \\&quot;kappa_1:\\&quot;, -0.11661807580174927113702623906705539359$\\grave{ }$12.}&quot;}</small></span></div></div></div>",
