  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (diagonal frame; $h=1/2$, $\\theta=2/7$, $z=(3/2,5/4,2/3)$, $w=(5/2,7/3,3/5)$).**\n- **Frame maps.** Exact: $P_{\\rm phys}\\,t^G(z)P_{\\rm phys}^{-1}=\\sum_iz_i\\mathcal L_{ii}$ and $P_{\\rm phys}\\,t^G(w)P_{\\rm phys}^{-1}=$ `tGPzw`, and $\\Omega_{zw}$ is its eigencovector with eigenvalue $\\tau_{\\rm vac}(w)$.\n- **The $w$-vacuum.** It is the $w$-state with $t_1=\\tau_{\\rm vac}(w)$ exactly. Its $Q$-degrees are direct $(0,1,2)$ and dual $(2,1,0)$, the weight-$(2,1,0)$ state.\n- **The match.** For all 8 $z$-states, with $|\\Omega_{zw}\\cdot\\Psi|\\ge0.6$,\n$$\\Omega_{zw}\\cdot\\Psi_{{\\rm diag},B}=\\big(\\Omega_{zw}P_{\\rm phys}\\cdot y_0\\big)\\,\\frac{\\det N\\big[Q^j_{B,z},\\,Q_{i,{\\rm vac},w}\\big]}{c_0\\langle x_0|y_0\\rangle\\,\\Psi_Q^{B,z}(x_0)\\,\\Phi_Q^{{\\rm vac},w}(y_0)}$$\n  to about $10^{-53}$. Here $\\Psi_{{\\rm diag},B}=P_{\\rm phys}|\\Psi_{B,z}\\rangle$ with $\\langle x_0|\\Psi_{B,z}\\rangle=1$.\n\nSo the overlap of the rotated twist-$w$ vacuum with any diagonal-frame twist-$z$ eigenstate is the functional determinant. The only state-dependent input is the $z$-state's own $Q$'s, in $\\det N$ and $\\Psi_Q(x_0)$; the vacuum contributes its own simple $Q_{i,{\\rm vac},w}$. The prefactor $\\Omega_{zw}P_{\\rm phys}\\cdot y_0$ is the normalization of the vacuum bra; it depends on $z$ and $w$ but not on the state.\n\nA bug fixed along the way: the vacuum selection used `Ordering` on a list that could contain `-Infinity`, which is $\\max$ of the empty coefficient list of an exactly-zero polynomial. `Ordering` sorts `-Infinity` after numbers, so the wrong state was picked. The cell now floors the max at 0.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
 "metadata": {
  "createdBy": "wolfbook_newNotebook",
  "createdAt": "2026-10-01T08:20:24.325Z"
 }
}